            "name": "submit_note",
            "input": {
              "body": "Corella Fresh Foods Pty Ltd passes all three covenants for the test period ending 30 September 2026, but net leverage and interest cover are on watch with thin headroom.\n\nNet leverage: 3.41x tested against a 3.50x maximum, headroom 2.7%. Calculated as (total debt 18.90m less cash 1.15m) divided by TTM EBITDA of 5.21m.\n\nInterest cover: 2.43x tested against a 2.25x minimum, headroom 8.2%. Calculated as TTM EBITDA of 5.21m divided by TTM interest expense of 2.14m.\n\nMinimum liquidity: 3.45m tested against a 3.00m minimum, headroom 15%. Cash plus undrawn revolver.\n\nThe compliance certificate reports 3.41x, 2.43x and 3,450k, all marked Complies. These agree with the tested values, and no disagreements were found.\n\nReview issue: cash at bank fell 39% from 1.87m (30 June 2026) to 1.15m (30 September 2026). The pack does not explain this beyond the commentary on higher working capital and a 1.2m revolver draw in August.\n\nContext: management says TTM EBITDA is now 5.2m, September gross margin was the lowest this year, and capex has been deferred.\n\nRecommended action: analyst to review the cash movement and request the working capital explanation and November revolver repayment evidence. Consider a forward-looking leverage and interest cover sensitivity, given the watch status."
            },
            "caller": {
              "type": "direct"
            }
          }
