            "type": "text",
            "text": "The September 2026 monitoring run for Corella Fresh Foods is saved as a note for analyst review. All three covenants pass, but net leverage and interest cover are both on watch.\n\n| Covenant | Tested | Limit | Headroom | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Net leverage | 3.41x | max 3.50x | 2.7% | Watch |\n| Interest cover | 2.43x | min 2.25x | 8.2% | Watch |\n| Minimum liquidity | $3.45m | min $3.00m | 15% | Pass |\n\n- **Certificate:** The borrower's compliance certificate reports the same three figures and claims compliance on each. The tested values agree with it.\n- **Review issue:** Cash at bank fell 39%, from $1.87m at 30 June to $1.15m at 30 September. The pack does not explain it beyond the commentary on higher working capital and a $1.2m revolver draw in August.\n- **Recommended action:** The analyst should ask for the working capital explanation and evidence of the November revolver repayment. A forward-looking sensitivity on leverage and interest cover is also worth considering, given how thin the headroom is.\n\nAll six extracted figures were accepted on the first submission, and all three certificate claims were accepted."
